# The build context for debian/Dockerfile, and only for it: BuildKit prefers a
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` over the repository root's when one exists.
#
# It differs from the root's in two ways: `debian/` is in, because this is the
# image that packages it, and only one path under `deploy/` is -- the landing
# page, which `debian/rules` installs into kerbridge-broker. Both deployments
# ship that one file, so neither holds a copy.
#
# `.git/` is deliberately *not* in. The version comes from KB_VERSION, derived
# on the host by `debian/make-changelog --print-version` and passed as a build
# arg, so this build needs no repository metadata at all -- an export or a
# release tarball packages the same as a checkout. It also costs 22 MB of
# context and a cache miss on every commit, which is a price worth paying only
# by an image nothing else is built from.
*
!LICENSE
!CHANGELOG.md
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates/
!debian/
!deploy/caddy/site/

# Build output, on both sides of the handover: cargo's, and the tree
# debian/stage-prebuilt fills inside the image.
crates/**/target/
debian/prebuilt/
debian/changelog
debian/kerbridge-config.NEWS
**/.local-tmp/
